## 3. SUPPLY CHAIN EXECUTION: GRN "VIEW ACCOUNTING" SHOWS NOTHING

**Defect:** GRN/receipt rows show status Posted, but View Accounting is empty. This means status was set to Posted without running the posting engine (likely in the seed and/or the status update code).

Fix it properly:
1. **Status must be derived from the engine.** A receipt can be "Posted" only through `createAccounting()` + `postToGL()`; it must store its `subledgerEntryId` and `glJournalId`. Remove any code path that sets Posted directly.
2. **Receipt flow with maker–checker:** Draft → Pending Approval → Approved → Posted (Noah Bennett creates; Charlotte approves; on approval the engine posts automatically). A receipt can be created only against an **Approved PO** and cannot exceed the open PO quantity (tolerance 0%).
3. **Accounting per the template:** stock items Dr Inventory (1200/1210/1220/1230 by item class) / Cr GRNI 2010, valued at PO price; services/non-stock per PO receipt-matching flag; the BU on every line is the receiving BU.
4. **View Accounting button on every supply-chain document** (Receipt, Stock Transfer, Consumption, Inventory Adjustment) opens a panel/table with the subledger lines (Account, Description, BU, Debit, Credit), totals, the **GL journal number as a link**, and posting date. For documents not yet posted show "Accounting will be created on approval" with a preview of the expected lines.
5. **Repair existing data (one-time migration + corrected seed):** find every receipt, transfer, consumption and adjustment that is Posted/Received without an accounting entry and generate the correct entries and GL journals using the original document date (flag the journals as `Source: Seed Repair` in the audit log; this is allowed to post into already-closed seed periods). Update `Reset Demo Data` so the seed always routes these documents through the engine.
6. Add these checks to the **System Integrity Check** page: (a) no Posted document without a GL journal, in any module; (b) GRNI balance = value of received-but-uninvoiced receipt lines; (c) inventory subledger value = GL 1200–1230 by BU.
7. Also verify that **Inventory On-hand** and the item cost update when a receipt is posted, and that the AP invoice matched to that receipt clears GRNI (Dr 2010 / Dr 5040 PPV / Dr 1400 / Cr 2000).

